{"duration_api_ms":121119,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a","total_cost_usd":0.8762698,"usage":{"input_tokens":46,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42646,"cache_read_input_tokens":1419389,"output_tokens":12552,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2311},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42646,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1192,"cache_read_input_tokens":74501,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":399},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":46,"outputTokens":12552,"cacheReadInputTokens":1419389,"cacheCreationInputTokens":42646,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8762698,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2311,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":42646,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_013H8jqoXiaRkCat4Hiw4bQd","tool_input":{"command":"S=/tmp/claude-0/-home-claude-euro-office-server-theseus-worktrees-PKT-0069/0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a/scratchpad; C=$S/eo/sdkjs/cell; chmod u+w $C; for f in sdk-all-min.js sdk-all.js; do rm $C/$f; cp /var/www/euro-office/documentserver/sdkjs/cell/$f $C/; done; rm $C/sdk-all.cache $C/sdk-all.bin; chmod u+w $C/*.js; ls -la $C; grep -o 'measureString=function[^}]\\{0,600\\}' $C/sdk-all-min.js | head -3; grep -c '' $C/sdk-all-min.js"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":23,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I built the shaping cache on a local copy of sdkjs and it is worth keeping: x2t used about 16–26 % less CPU converting large xlsx files to pdf. Every page of the 25k-row PDF comes out pixel-identical. My recommendation is a small patch applied in the sdkjs source or sent upstream, not a broad fork.\n\n**Results** (CPU seconds; one or two runs each on a shared VM, native 9.3.7-1 package):\n\n| Sample | Before | With cache |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 sheet, 25k rows (2 runs) | 19.8 / 18.7 | 16.5 / 15.6 |\n| 1 sheet, 50k rows | 36.8 | 30.9 |\n| 1 sheet, 50k rows, numbers only | 42.3 | 31.3 |\n\n- **Memory:** peak memory grows by 50–90 MB (cache capped at 200,000 entries).\n- **Output:** all 521 pages of the 25k-row PDF render pixel-identical to the original; the PDF files differ only in metadata.\n- **Why the gain is partial:** the cache removes roughly a quarter to a third of the shaping cost, not all of it. In these samples about half the columns (ids, prices, totals) hold near-unique values, so they never hit the cache.\n\n**What I did**\n- **Setup:** I ran x2t against a copy of the install in my scratch directory, with the converter's `bin` folder copied over, so the installed files were never touched.\n- **The patch:** `.theseus/oracle/perf/sdkjs-shape-cache.py` adds about 15 lines that cache the result of `FragmentShaper.shapeFragment`, keyed by font name, size, bold/italic, resolution and text. On a repeat it reuses the stored glyphs and widths instead of shaping the text again, so it cannot change the layout.\n- **Not tested:** skipping measurement for numbers that fit. That changes how cells overflow or show `###`, so it would need visual regression tests first.\n\n**Surprises**\n- x2t runs `sdkjs/cell/sdk-all.js`. The `sdk-all-min.js` named in the packet does not contain this code.\n- Moving `sdk-all.bin` and `sdk-all.cache` (the V8 snapshot and code cache) out of my copy did not change the CPU time.\n\n**Not done**\n- I did not count cache hits, because x2t gives the patched code no way to print anything.\n- I did not re-measure after rebuilding the V8 snapshot.\n\n**Follow-up:** I recorded a request in `.theseus/spawn/` (needs `documentserver`) to port the cache into the sdkjs source (`cell/view/StringRender.js`), rebuild the snapshot, and measure again.\n\nThe packet lists no acceptance commands. `theseus validate` reports 0 errors and 1 warning, which I did not look into. The work is committed with the write-up in `.theseus/diagnosis/PKT-0069-shape-cache.md`, the Executor log, Lessons for the Atlas, and the friction line.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- To run x2t against a patched sdkjs, copy the install with `server/FileConverter/bin` as real files. The config's `../../../sdkjs` path then points at your copy.\n- The patch goes in `sdkjs/cell/sdk-all.js`, not `sdk-all-min.js`.\n- Caching text shaping cuts xlsx-to-pdf CPU by 16–26 % with identical output. Columns of unique numbers still miss the cache.","ttft_ms":2442,"type":"result","duration_ms":536853,"uuid":"868b48ae-303e-4060-a8d3-437ed462f613","ttft_stream_ms":1133,"time_to_request_ms":445,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":249,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":27,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":16,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":9,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":17,"query_setup":9,"auto_mode_context_wait":16,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":45,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":8,"request_build":16},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":92,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":214,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"p